   <pb xml:id="leaf001r" facs="loc_gk.01388_large.jpg" type="recto"/>
   
   <head type="main" rend="tripleUnderline">An Indian Bureau Reminiscence</head>
   <byline rend="underline">By Walt Whitman</byline>
   
   <p>
    <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">At</del><add place="above" seq="2">After</add></subst> the close of the <hi rend="tripleUnderline" hand="#h02">S</hi>ecession
    <hi rend="tripleUnderline" hand="#h02">w</hi>ar in '65 I worked
    <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">for</del> several months, (until Mr.
    Harlan turned me out for writing
    "Leaves of Grass,") in the Interior
    Department at Washington,
    in the Indian Bureau. Along
    this time <add place="below" rend="marked"><metamark target="#a001" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a001">there came to <del rend="overstrike">Washington to</del> see their <hi rend="tripleUnderline">G</hi>reat <hi rend="tripleUnderline">F</hi>ather,</add> an unusual number
    of <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">Indian</del><add place="above" seq="2">aboriginal</add></subst> visitors delegations
    for treaties, settlement of lands,<add place="below"><metamark target="#a002" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a002">&amp;c.,</add>&#8212;
    <milestone unit="glued"/>
    <del rend="overstrike" seq="1">groups of <gap reason="illegible" extent="one word" resp="#ja"/></del><add place="above" seq="2">&#8212;some</add> young and middle
    aged, <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">and some</del><add place="above" seq="2">but mainly</add></subst> old men, from the
    West, North, and occasionally from
    the South&#8212;<add place="below" rend="marked"><metamark target="#a003" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a003">&#8212;several hundreds of them, in parties of from <gap reason="illegible" extent="one word" resp="#ja"/> twenty <gap reason="illegible" extent="one word" resp="#ja"/></add>the most wonderful <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1"><gap reason="illegible" extent="one word" resp="#ja"/></del><add place="above" seq="2">proofs</add></subst>
    of what <hi rend="tripleUnderline">N</hi>ature can produce,
    <milestone unit="glued"/>
    (the survival of the fittest, no doubt,
    <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">and the</del><add place="above" seq="2">all the</add></subst> frailer samples, sorted out,
    by death)&#8212;how the earth and woods
    the attrition of storms and elements
    can train and fashion, and what
    they can turn out indeed <hi rend="underline">chiefs</hi>,
    men
   </p>

